hw/sh4: ze0 HPB-DMAC for the SD data path, SD card lock, debug SCIF alias (TODO M8.C1b).

hw/sh4/ze0_hpbdmac.c (new): the HPB-DMAC at 0xffc08000 (nk.exe, P4) and
its area-7 alias 0x1fc08000 (SDHC.dll through VirtualCopy).  Evidence
(EU2011 build B): SDHC.dll fn 0x039be010 builds the register pointers
(0x40 bytes per channel, port 0 = channel 8, port 1 = channel 9; common
+0x80c/+0x810/+0x814); nk.exe's interrupt rows for channels 8/9 (INTEVT
0xc60 fn 0x8803e7f8, 0xc80 fn 0x8803e850) clear the channel bit of +0x814
and set the port's "DMA done" byte, and OEMInterruptDone fn 0x8803e004
ORs the bit into +0x810 and +0x814.  So +0x80c = interrupt status, +0x810
= clear, +0x814 = enable; channel +0x00/+0x04/+0x08 = source,
destination, count, +0x28 = control, +0x2c bit 0 = enable, +0x30 = stop,
+0x34 bit 0 = running (the layout of the Renesas HPB-DMAC).  Only the two
SD channels move data: when the channel is enabled and the SD host has a
transfer in DMA mode, the bytes are copied between the card and guest RAM
at once, the count goes to 0, the status bit is set and the interrupt
asserts while enabled.  The count unit is 2 bytes with control bit 8
(16-bit beats) times 8 with bit 21 (burst): observed 0x00202100 / 4 for
64 bytes, 0x00002100 / 4 for 8 bytes.  hpbdmac-trace=on logs every
register access and each transfer (bytes, guest address, CRC-32, first 16
bytes) under -d unimp.  Other channels (the serial drivers program 1, 3,
7 and 10) are register storage only.

hw/sh4/ze0_sdhi.c: DMA side of SD_BUF0 (ze0_sdhi_dma_read/write, a kick
when a transfer starts in DMA mode; BRE/BWE raise no interrupt then).
Fix: SD_BUF0 was gated by the BRE/BWE status bit, which the driver clears
before it touches the buffer, so its first PIO write (CMD42) was dropped;
the gate is now the transfer state.  sdhi-trace logs the first word of a
PIO write block (for CMD42: mode byte and length, never the password).

hw/sh4/ze0_intc.c: sources HPBDMAC8/9 at INTEVT 0xc60/0xc80, INT2 bit 19
(every HPB-DMAC ISR masks and unmasks it; INT2 +0x3c reads it back),
level fixed at the table's IntrPrio 14 (the INT2PRI field is not located).

hw/sh4/ze0.c: machine options hpbdmac (default on; off = negative
control, the first data transfer times out), hpbdmac-trace, sd-pwd-tofu
(default on) and sd-start-locked; an area-7 alias for the debug SCIF
(channel 6): once the card is unlocked serial_scif.dll opens it and spun
in fn 0x0398e888 on SCFSR.TEND through the unassigned 0x1fe46010.

hw/sd/sd.c (QEMU's card model): (1) CMD6: a group argument 0xF ("no
influence") reported 0xF in the status, which means "error"; it now
reports the function the group keeps (SDHC.dll rejected the card).  (2)
CMD42: a password of the stored length was refused ("<=" for "<").  (3)
new sd-card properties pwd-tofu and start-locked: the card has a CMD42
password, namely the first one a host presents ("trust on first use").
The head unit refuses a card with no password, and the password is
unit-specific and must not be in the repository; with pwd-tofu the
firmware's own LOCK and UNLOCK both succeed against QEMU's lock logic
without the patch knowing a byte of it.

Evidence and controls: docs/experiments/EXP-2026-11-21-M8.C1b-hpb-dmac-model.md
(C-6870..C-6879).  Base: QEMU 8.2.10 + the earlier patches (sorts after
ze0-0008).

This file is the QEMU 11.1.3 form of the patch (TODO M8.A11): the text
above was written for the 8.2 series, where the patch was first made;
API names in it that 11.x renamed are listed in PORT-11.1.md.  Base: tag
v11.1.3 plus the earlier patches of this directory, in sorted order.

